# Icons

Do not design or draw icons. No hand-written SVG pictograms, no invented paths, no “simple” stand-in glyphs.

Use [Material Symbols](https://fonts.google.com/icons) Outlined. Add only the names you need on the existing Google Fonts stylesheet, `icon_names` in alphabetical order:

```html
<link
  href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Material+Symbols+Outlined:opsz,wght,FILL,GRAD@24,400,0,0&icon_names=pets,train&display=block"
  rel="stylesheet"
/>
```

```jsx
<span className="material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">
  train
</span>
```

The ligature text is the official icon name (`train`, `pets`, `waves`). If Material Symbols has no glyph for a concept, pick the closest existing name. Do not draw a replacement.

The Fieldy logo lockup is a brand mark, not an icon. Leave `electron/renderer/fieldy-logo.svg` and the inline logo SVG alone.
